            "id": 3,
            "type": "markdown",
            "source": "> **Why LangGraph has *RetryPolicy* on a node**\n>\n> Every tool could wrap itself in a retry loop, but then each author decides differently and side effects get retried by accident. Declaring the policy on the node gives one rule for all tools in it, keeps tool code plain, and lets you say precisely which errors are transient."
