          "idea": "Independent checks should not wait for each other. Several edges from one node run branches at the same time, a reducer (operator.add) merges their writes to the shared key, and a fan-in node waits for all of them. Send creates such branches at run time, one per item.",
          "example": "Three colleagues check attendance, credits and prerequisites at the same desk simultaneously, then drop their notes into one tray for the decision.",
